WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.208
This is FormBridge, a restaurant enquiry desk for staff. We'll follow Alex's

00:00:05.208 --> 00:00:10.416
birthday dinner, from a voice message to a handoff for the next

00:00:10.416 --> 00:00:10.850
shift.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.738
Start with your own conversation. You can type customer and staff messages,

00:00:16.738 --> 00:00:21.977
paste a conversation, or open voice input to record or upload a

00:00:21.977 --> 00:00:22.850
short message.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.686
The voice message becomes an editable transcript. Check names, dates and numbers.

00:00:28.686 --> 00:00:33.871
Use in composer places the words in the message box; it does

00:00:33.871 --> 00:00:35.600
not submit them automatically.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:41.510
Add the reviewed message. FormBridge gathers the restaurant, city, date, time and

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:46.770
guest count. Alex's first request is four guests at Juniper in Sydney,

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.400
at seven thirty in the evening.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:55.512
Alex changes the request to five guests, sometime after eight. The guest

00:00:55.512 --> 00:01:00.974
count updates. The time stays open, with a specific question to ask

00:01:00.974 --> 00:01:03.250
rather than an invented answer.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:09.344
Staff suggests eight thirty. Once Alex accepts, the brief can use that

00:01:09.344 --> 00:01:14.789
exact time. Open the time detail to see both the suggestion and

00:01:14.789 --> 00:01:16.150
the customer's acceptance.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.750
The desk assistant works with the enquiry. Ask for a follow-up to

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:24.700
check the vegetarian request and a note for the next shift. Each

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.650
action is a proposal. Apply it when you are happy with it.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:34.665
Add guest-care details: a name, contact details if needed, dietary requests, seating

00:01:34.665 --> 00:01:40.029
and the occasion. These are staff notes, separate from the five booking

00:01:40.029 --> 00:01:44.500
details. Requests still need checking with the guest and restaurant.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:50.470
Review the sources and approve the brief. Save it to this device

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:55.790
or your private team workspace. FormBridge prepares an enquiry; it does not

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.450
check availability or reserve a table.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:04.411
Continue on this device to create a private workspace. Invite teammates with

00:02:04.411 --> 00:02:09.722
a code. Team cases are visible to members, and conflicting saved edits

00:02:09.722 --> 00:02:11.050
require another review.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:17.047
Open the service planner. Choose a saved service date to see the

00:02:17.047 --> 00:02:22.394
enquiries in time order, including known guest counts and dietary requests. Unfinished

00:02:22.394 --> 00:02:26.850
dates stay out of the timeline until they are agreed.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:32.765
The follow-up queue keeps the next step visible. Mark a task complete

00:02:32.765 --> 00:02:38.029
when the work is done. Copy or download a shift handoff, and

00:02:38.029 --> 00:02:41.100
reopen the enquiry whenever the conversation changes.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:46.617
That's FormBridge: the conversation, the details and the next step in one

00:02:46.617 --> 00:02:51.483
place. Bring your own restaurant enquiry, and give the next shift a

00:02:51.483 --> 00:02:52.700
clearer starting point.
